:::card title="The Drowned Lantern"
<style>
  .lantern {
    max-width: 420px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 14px;
    background: #1a120b;
    border: 2px solid #3d2b1f;
    border-radius: 6px;
    font-family: Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;
    color: #d9c8a9;
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 40px rgba(0,0,0,0.8), 0 0 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.6);
  }
  .sign {
    text-align: center;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #3d2b1f;
    padding-bottom: 10px;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }
  .sign h1 {
    font-size: 20px;
    letter-spacing: 2px;
    color: #b8915a;
    margin: 0;
    text-shadow: 0 0 12px rgba(184,145,90,0.4);
  }
  .sign .sub {
    font-size: 11px;
    font-style: italic;
    color: #8a7554;
    margin-top: 4px;
  }
  .menu {
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    border-top: 1px dashed #3d2b1f;
    padding-top: 8px;
  }
  .menu .row {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
  }
  .menu .row span:first-child { color: #cbb894; }
  .menu .row span:last-child { color: #8a7554; }
  .stamped {
    margin-top: 12px;
    text-align: center;
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 3px;
    color: #5a4630;
    border: 1px solid #3d2b1f;
    padding: 4px;
    transform: rotate(-2deg);
    opacity: 0.7;
  }
  .smoke {
    position: relative;
  }
  .smoke::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background: radial-gradient(ellipse at 30% 20%, rgba(180,160,120,0.08), transparent 60%);
    pointer-events: none;
  }
</style>
<div class="lantern smoke">
  <div class="sign">
    <h1>THE DROWNED LANTERN</h1>
    <div class="sub">ale · stew · no questions</div>
  </div>
  <div class="menu">
    <div class="row"><span>Bitter Ale (choked with brine)</span><span>2d</span></div>
    <div class="row"><span>Dockmaster's Stew</span><span>6d</span></div>
    <div class="row"><span>Salted Herring, cold</span><span>3d</span></div>
    <div class="row"><span>Room — back of house, one night</span><span>12d</span></div>
  </div>
  <div class="stamped">NO WATCH BUSINESS AFTER DARK</div>
</div>
:::

The taproom smells of brine, damp wool, and woodsmoke. A dozen faces flicker up from shadowed stools — fishermen, riggers, a couple of women in oilskins who drop their eyes back down too fast. The barmaid, a heavy-browed girl with rope burns on her forearms, gives you a once-over and a crooked grin, not quite a smile.

"Marro's in the back room," she says, sliding a mug of something dark and bitter onto the bar as if you'd already ordered. "Mind the door. It's stuck worse than the tide."

Beyond the curtain that flaps in the draft, a low murmur reaches you — two or three voices, speaking soft, plus the wet sound of a pipe being relit.

:::card title="Wanted — by order of the Harbourmaster"
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Wanted Poster</title>
<style>
    :root {
        --parchment: #d4c5a3;
        --ink: #2b2622;
        --accent: #5c1a14;
    }
    body {
        margin: 0;
        min-height: 100vh;
        display: flex;
        justify-content: center;
        align-items: center;
        background: radial-gradient(circle at center, #333 0%, #111 100%);
        font-family: 'Georgia', serif;
    }
    .poster {
        width: 280px;
        padding: 20px 15px;
        background-color: var(--parchment);
        background-image: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(139, 69, 19, 0.1) 0%, transparent 100%);
        color: var(--ink);
        text-align: center;
        position: relative;
        box-shadow: 0 10px 30px rgba(0,0,0,0.5);
        transform: rotate(-2deg);
        clip-path: polygon(0% 2%, 5% 0%, 15% 3%, 25% 1%, 35% 3%, 45% 0%, 55% 2%, 65% 0%, 75% 2%, 85% 0%, 95% 3%, 100% 2%, 99% 50%, 100% 98%, 90% 100%, 80% 97%, 70% 100%, 60% 98%, 50% 100%, 40% 97%, 30% 100%, 20% 98%, 10% 100%, 0% 97%);
    }
    .poster::before {
        content: '';
        position: absolute;
        top: 0; left: 0; right: 0; bottom: 0;
        background-image: url('data:image/svg+xml;utf8,<svg width="100" height="100" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M10 10 L110 110 M110 10 L10 110" stroke="rgba(0,0,0,0.03)" stroke-width="2"/></svg>');
        pointer-events: none;
    }
    .header {
        font-size: 2.5rem;
        font-weight: bold;
        color: var(--accent);
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: 5px;
        margin-bottom: 10px;
        text-shadow: 1px 1px 0px rgba(255,255,255,0.2);
    }
    .divider {
        border: none;
        border-top: 3px solid var(--ink);
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--ink);
        margin: 10px 0;
        height: 5px;
    }
    .portrait {
        width: 120px;
        height: 150px;
        margin: 0 auto 15px auto;
        border: 2px dashed rgba(43, 38, 34, 0.5);
        background: #c8b997;
        position: relative;
        display: flex;
        justify-content: center;
        align-items: flex-end;
    }
    .face {
        width: 60px;
        height: 80px;
        background: rgba(0,0,0,0.2);
        border-radius: 30px 30px 10px 10px;
    }
    .face::after {
        content: '??';
        position: absolute;
        top: 30px;
        font-size: 2rem;
        color: rgba(0,0,0,0.3);
        font-style: italic;
    }
    .name {
        font-size: 1.2rem;
        font-weight: bold;
        margin: 5px 0;
    }
    .desc {
        font-size: 0.85rem;
        line-height: 1.3;
        font-style: italic;
        margin-bottom: 15px;
    }
    .reward {
        border: 2px solid var(--accent);
        padding: 5px;
        margin: 10px 0;
        display: inline-block;
    }
    .reward span {
        display: block;
        font-size: 0.7rem;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: 2px;
    }
    .reward strong {
        display: block;
        font-size: 1.4rem;
        color: var(--accent);
    }
    .footer {
        font-size: 0.65rem;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: 1px;
        margin-top: 10px;
    }
    .seal {
        position: absolute;
        bottom: 15px;
        right: 15px;
        width: 40px;
        height: 40px;
        background: radial-gradient(circle, var(--accent) 60%, transparent 60%);
        opacity: 0.6;
        border-radius: 50%;
        border: 1px solid var(--accent);
        display: flex;
        justify-content: center;
        align-items: center;
        color: var(--parchment);
        font-size: 0.5rem;
        transform: rotate(15deg);
    }
</style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="poster">
        <div class="header">Wanted</div>
        <div class="portrait"><div class="face"></div></div>
        <div class="name">Marro</div>
        <div class="divider"></div>
        <div class="desc">
            Fence of stolen goods. Known alias: "The Gull."<br>
            Last seen in the Drowned Lantern.
        </div>
        <div class="reward">
            <span> Reward </span>
            <strong>500 Crowns</strong>
        </div>
        <div class="footer">
            By order of the Harbourmaster<br>
            Dead or Alive
        </div>
        <div class="seal">HS</div>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
:::
The smell hits you before the sight — salt-cured air, spilled ale, and the sharp bite of wet wool. The Drowned Lantern is a low-ceilinged hole in the wall that serves as a bar to the honest folk upstairs and a den for the dishonest below. A painted lantern hangs from a beam, leaking water onto a cask below, and the sound of a fiddle being played terribly cuts through the murmur of low conversation.

You’re scanning the crowd, but you don’t need to look long. Everyone knows who the fence is, and everyone knows he’s here. Marro is sitting in the darkest corner booth, a mountain of a man wrapped in a coat that costs more than your yearly wage. He’s peeling a hard-boiled egg, the white skin curling off in long strips, and he’s looking directly at you with the flat, unblinking gaze of a cat watching a mouse. He doesn't smile. In the corner of the room, a wanted poster is pinned to the wall — "Marro" — though the face is a blur. He’s just a name now, a story, and a fence with a habit of chewing eggshells.

Marro sets the egg down on the table and wipes his greasy hands on a handkerchief that does little to help. "You’re dripping on the floor," he says, his voice a low rumble that carries over the noise. "And you’re the only one who hasn't paid a drink. If you're here to buy, you know the rules. If you're here to talk... well, talk costs more than gold these days." He looks at the door, then back at you. "What do you want, Rook?"

:::card title="The Drowned Lantern — Booth Table"
<table class="note">
<tr><th colspan="3">Saltmere Courier's Mark</th></tr>
<tr><td class="sig">Seal: Harbor Guild of Tides</td><td colspan="2" class="sub">Delivered in hand · do not open before the Lantern's own ink</td></tr>
<tr><td class="num">Forty gold</td><td class="num">Paid in full</td><td class="due">Witness: M.</td></tr>
</table>
<style>
.note{font-family:Georgia,serif;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#efe3c2,#d9c79b);color:#3b2a15;border:2px solid #8a6a3b;width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center}
.note th,.note td{padding:4px 6px;border:1px solid #b59a68;font-size:12px}
.sig{font-style:italic}
.sub{font-size:10px;color:#6b5730}
.num{font-weight:bold}
.due{color:#7a1f1f;font-weight:bold}
</style>
:::

Marro slides the sealed satchel across the scarred wood and turns the wax over, studying the courier's mark the way a man examines a fish for rot. "Clean seal. Harbor guild, no cracks. That's a good thing, Rook." He grins, ink bleeding off his fingers onto the table. "Which means whoever paid you to carry it was paying well. Which means I owe you more than you think."

He leans in, dropping his voice beneath the clatter of the taproom. "Forty gold's your cut, as agreed. But there's something in that satchel I'd pay you to *not* open. You trust me?" He taps the table twice, a nervous tick. "Tell me what the seal looks like under the ink, and I'll know I'm safe."
